Rebased this PR onto `dev` at `755ebdb94e` and resolved one test-only migration conflict while preserving both the new upstream migration-history coverage and the read-only inspection coverage from this branch.

The first six commits carried forward from #36710 remain attributed to @chubes4. #36710 was closed by automated stale-PR cleanup; it was not merged or technically rejected.

Post-rebase validation:

- changed UI tests: 2/2 passed;
- changed Core maintenance/migration/compaction tests: 28/28 passed;
- changed OpenCode background-job/HttpApi/analysis/progress tests: 23/23 passed;
- prompt/task consumers: 101 passed, 1 expected skip;
- v2 session runner: 87/87 passed;
- storage HttpApi effect exercise: 8/8 passed;
- app, Core, OpenCode, schema, generated SDK, and client typechecks passed;
- generated SDK/client rebuilds produced no diff;
- changed-file formatting/lint and `git diff --check` passed.

#43456 looks complementary rather than duplicative: it provides smaller CLI stats/prune/Vacuum helpers and removes orphaned event rows, while this PR also compacts superseded snapshots for live sessions and adds UI/progress, verified-backup requirements, and process coordination. I updated the PR description to make that relationship explicit.

Thanks @XiaoTong6666 for the 10 GB database data point. The repeated full-snapshot updates you measured are exactly the class of reclaimable history targeted here.

Ready for review.
